Rombie's change to Stella (Bro Code Technologies, 2026-10-29), under Stella's GPL-2.0-or-later, for Stella 7.0c
(c4016ea), in four parts.

1. The core is built without the code Stella says it took from z26, whose license (the GPL "Version 2", with no
   "or any later version") cannot be combined with RetroArch's GPL-3.0. Removed:
   - the CompuMate (cartridge scheme CM and its keyboard): a CompuMate cartridge no longer loads;
   - the Kid Vid, the MindLink, the Amiga mouse, the Atari mouse and the trackball: a game set to one of them gets a
     joystick;
   - the mouse driving a joystick, and the trackball sensitivity setting;
   - the z26 palette: choosing it gives Stella's standard palette, and the libretro option no longer offers it;
   - the default Supercharger header: a 6K image now gets one written from the load format's fields.
   stella/build.sh also deletes the removed classes' files (CartCM, CompuMate, KidVid, MindLink, PointingDevice,
   AmigaMouse, AtariMouse, TrakBall) from the build's copy, so nothing compiled can include them.
2. Every string stream's .view() becomes .str(), in the 25 files the build compiles that call it. Emscripten 3.1.46,
   the toolchain every Rombie engine is built with, ships libc++ 16, which has no basic_stringstream::view()
   (libc++ 17). str() returns the same text as a string; every result goes into a string or straight into a call.
3. On Emscripten, starting emulation clears the input events at once instead of 0.5 s later on TimerManager's thread:
   the Emscripten build has no threads, and creating one threw an exception nothing caught, so no game loaded.
4. Backported to the libretro port from Stella's later one (Stella's master, #1083), adapted to 7.0c:
   - a stick turns a paddle relatively (the dial moves at a speed set by how far the stick is pushed and stays where
     it is when let go), with the options stella_paddle_analog_absolute (disabled: relative; enabled: 7.0c's
     behaviour) and stella_paddle_analog_deadzone (default 15%); each paddle reads its own pad's left stick, where
     7.0c read the second paddle of a port from a pad's right stick;
   - a stick steers the driving controller (LeftDrivingAnalog, RightDrivingAnalog);
   - the port devices Joystick, Paddles and Driving (RETRO_DEVICE_SUBCLASS of the joypad, 0, 4 and 5, numbered as
     in the later port) put that controller on the first two ports in place of the game database's choice, through
     Stella's own "lc" and "rc" settings, and a change starts the game again. The joypad device itself is
     "Automatic (from ROM database)".

